  - Added a **Skipped** KPI to the dashboard header (all-time total from
    `SUM(runs.jobs_skipped)`, so it counts historical runs too).

- [x] **New "Skipped" tab — how many were skipped, why, + lots of graphs**
  - New **⏭️ Skipped** tab (`dashboard/app.py :: _skipped_section`):
    - Metrics: skip events · distinct reasons · most common reason
    - **Why jobs were skipped** — reason breakdown (bar chart)
    - **Skips over time** — per-day trend (line chart)
    - Breakdowns **by company / workplace type / experience level** (bar charts)
    - Full per-job **detail table** with a clickable job link
    - A plain-English **legend** explaining every reason code

- [x] **Clickable KPI cards → per-category focus drill-down**
  - The five header KPIs (applications today, total submitted, failed, skipped,
    jobs discovered) are now bordered **cards** with a **View details →** button.
  - Clicking one opens an inline drill-down (`_focus_panel`) under the header
    with category-specific charts (per-day trend line + top companies / résumé
    usage / workplace type / experience level / Easy Apply-vs-external bars) and
    a filtered record table with a clickable **Open ↗** job link. **✕ Close**
    dismisses it.
  - Query/aggregation is pure and Streamlit-free in `dashboard/focus.py`
    (`build_focus_view` → `FocusView` / `FocusChart`), unit-tested in
    `tests/test_focus.py` (8). `st.tabs` can't be switched programmatically, so
    the panel renders in place via `st.session_state["focus_category"]`.

### How it's wired (for reference)

- New `skips` table (`database/sql/schema.sql`) — one row per skip event,
  `(run_id, job_id, reason, created_at)`; kept separate from `applications`
  so it never affects submit / reapply / stats logic.
- `Database.record_skip()` + `Database.skip_events()` (LEFT JOIN to `jobs`).
- `Orchestrator._note_skip()` now counts **and** persists the reason at every
  skip site (gates, below-threshold, AI-advised, scan-only, reapply-open-failed,
  and form-level skipped/dry_run/aborted).
- Tests: `tests/test_skips.py` (9). Docs synced: README, ARCHITECTURE, INIT.MD,
  faq, data-structures, architecture (learning docs).

